     "result_text_tail": "e:** the board deciding to approve or reject. **Look:** the navy theme. I went ahead with the storyline without an approval step.\n- **Profit measure:** \"contribution after site costs\" is per-order profit after the dark store's fixed costs (rent, staff, utilities). The pack doesn't define contribution, so the deck uses this measure throughout.\n- **The $9.5M plan:** the pack doesn't say whether this includes the software business's own $0.4M-a-month burn. The chart assumes it does, which is the reading most favourable to the founders, and a sidebar note shows that the other reading runs out of cash before month 18.\n- **Software breakeven:** this estimate assumes revenue tracks recurring revenue, costs stay flat apart from the new hires, and 60% growth continues. The assumptions are listed on the slide.\n- **Survey versus pop-up:** the 44% weekly-use survey and the 22% retention figure measure different groups (local residents against acquired customers). A footnote says the comparison is only indicative.\n\n**Small display quirk:** outside the charts, the renderer rounds some dollar figures to one decimal, so a few cards show \u2212$6.2 or \u2212$1.1 next to \u2212$6.17 and \u2212$1.05 in the charts. Where it matters, the caption gives the exact figure.\n\nI can switch the theme if you want, for example to `mono`, which prints well in black and white.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- parcelbird-now.pptx\n- parcelbird-now-sources.xlsx\n\nThe spec and build script are in `./work/` if you want to re-render."
    }
